CSR Protocol-to-Section Population — Design Handoff
Author: Adam, Regulatory Medical Writing
Audience: Scribbler development team
Status: Manual prompt chain, prototype. Steps 1–3 run on a live protocol. Step 4 authored, not yet run.
1. What this does
Generates CSR section content derived from a study protocol, with every generated statement traceable to a specific protocol location.
The protocol is the only content source. A CSR file is used as a structural reference — to enumerate target sections — and is explicitly barred from acting as a source of content.
2. The core problem
Derivation fidelity. Every CSR statement must trace to a specific protocol locator, and content that is grounded (stated in the protocol) must be mechanically distinguishable from content that is inferred (required by the CSR but not present in the protocol).
This is the property the pipeline lives or dies on. If automation preserves nothing else from this design, it must preserve this.
3. The four steps
Each step produces a verified artifact before the next begins. Each seam is a human sign-off gate.
